  "design": {
    "decision": "Save a [♠] for the end and make sure the opponents lead trick 13: the team may deliberately lose trick 12 and void a side suit so the final lead comes into its trump.",
    "opponent": "Revealed when it fires. Opponents who suspect it hold back a [♠] of their own, or lead [♠] on trick 13 to deny the trump.",
    "rationale": "ua-spade-last-x was cut because winning the last trick with [♠] barely differs from winning it at all. 'By trumping' requires a non-[♠] lead on trick 13, which creates a real sequencing decision about losing trick 12. The trigger combines two existing fields of one trigger (last trick, by trumping), with no rider. A narrower condition earns the ×2.5 starting amount.",
